{Spin2_v50}
'' =================================================================================================
''
''   File....... test_bench_dual.spin2
''   Purpose.... Motion harness (task 3508, silo 5): speed law, deceleration curves, fault boundary,
''               clock sweep, bus ratio, distance overshoot, fault as seen from outside and the
''               wheels-down turn direction, measured from the driver's own telemetry only
''   Authors.... Stephen M Moraco
''               -- Copyright (c) 2026 Iron Sheep Productions, LLC
''               -- see below for terms of use
''   E-mail..... stephen@ironsheep.biz
''   Started.... 14 Sep 2026
''   Updated.... 14 Sep 2026 -- part b2: marks and windows located by ring index (sec 12.7); the
''               STOPMODE, LIVE, LADDER, CLOCK, FAULTB, OVERSHT, BASELINE and POSTFLT segments
''               14 Sep 2026 -- part b3: the attended OUTSIDE and FLOOR segments with the bmpanel
''               operator panel (assets and BM_* geometry from tools/gen_dual_assets.py); OVERSHT's
''               distance power set and printed from OVERSHT_POWER (sec 12.8, PL-51); the debug
''               record budget table below
''               14 Sep 2026 -- SRC_REV=4: the cable-swap part removed (no swap is possible on this rig,
''               and Visit 1 settled the field question); FLOOR_RUN_MS 2 s, a brief wheels-down
''               observation (design sec 12.1 Q1, Q10)
''               14 Sep 2026 -- SRC_REV=5: each clock build owns its sign-off cells, ids ending -K200 / -K270
''               / -K300 selected from CLK_FREQ; a CLOCK build at any other clock judges no cell (design
''               sec 12.10)
''               15 Sep 2026 -- SRC_REV=6: the attended panel names the braked wheel (LEFT, the P32 board),
''               counts down before the harness drives the wheels again and then shows HANDS CLEAR; part
''               UICHECK (-D DUAL_PART_UICHECK, tier dual-ui) walks the operator through every panel control
''               and every attended screen with no wheel or steering object ever started (STEPHEN 2026-09-15)
''
'' =================================================================================================

{ WHAT THIS BINARY IS

  Governing design: DOCs/plans/MOTION-HARNESS-DESIGN.md, with its section 12 arbiter rulings.

  NO EXTERNAL MEASUREMENT (STEPHEN 2026-09-14). Every reading comes from the driver's own status
  block, its calibrated sense channel and the hall inputs.

  ONE SOURCE, ONE PART PER BUILD. tools/bench-run.sh chooses the part with -D DUAL_PART_A,
  DUAL_PART_CLOCK, DUAL_PART_B, DUAL_PART_BRAKE, DUAL_PART_C, DUAL_PART_FLOOR or DUAL_PART_UICHECK.
  PART_ID comes from one #ifdef chain; with no part flag the build prints part NONE, runs no segment, and ends cleanly.

  COG MODEL
   - cog 0: runs every command and every emitter; never calls a library getter inside a timed wait.
   - instrument cog: samples both motors every INST_PERIOD_TICKS into one ring on one timebase. Its
     call graph holds no debug() statement (I1), it holds no lock, and it stops cooperatively (I4).
   - watchdog cog: watches cog 0's heartbeat; on a stall it stops wheelL, wheelR and steering, then
     ends the session (test_bench_scan.spin2's pattern, extended).

  INVARIANTS named in the design's section 1 (I1-I12) are cited where the code keeps them.

  RECORDS: tag-first BM- records, one debug(zstr_()) line each through emitRecord(), run-wide seq
  as the second field, every field clamped, worst case under 280 bytes (stated at each emitter).

  HOW IT IS RUN (from the repo root; each load adds -D BENCH_CFG -D BENCH_QUIET and its part flag)

      tools/bench-run.sh dual-a | dual-clock <clkfreq> | dual-b | dual-brake | dual-c | dual-floor | dual-ui

  DEBUG RECORD BUDGET (design sec 6.2). Ceiling: 255 debug records per compiled program.

    source                                         records  how counted
    test_bench_dual.spin2, records and markers           5  read: main() DEBUG_END_SESSION,
                                                            emitRecord(), the panic line in
                                                            emitHeaderRecords(), declareStall()
                                                            DEBUG_END_SESSION, wdEmitRecord()
    test_bench_dual.spin2, operator panel               16  read: panelSetup() 8 (PLOT, 5 x LAYER,
                                                            CROP 1, UPDATE); panelRender() 6 (prompt
                                                            CROP, state CROP, button CROP, button
                                                            restore CROP, digit CROP, UPDATE);
                                                            panelReadInput() 2 (PC_KEY, PC_MOUSE)
    isp_bench_log.spin2                                  0  read: no debug statement
    isp_bldc_motor.spin2 under the quiet masks          20  DEBUG-CHANNELS-DESIGN.md: ERROR 17 +
                                                            WARNING 3
    isp_steering_2wheel.spin2 under the quiet masks     10  DEBUG-CHANNELS-DESIGN.md: ERROR 10
    TOTAL, each object image counted once               51  of 255
    TOTAL, each of the four motor instances counted    111  of 255 (wheelL, wheelR and the steering
                                                            object's two, design sec 11 fact 9)

  The library rows hold only under -D BENCH_CFG -D BENCH_QUIET. The builds tools/build-check.sh makes
  without those flags enable more library channels; there, as for every build, the compiler accepting
  the program is the confirmation that the ceiling holds, and this table is the count, not a measurement.

  PANIC PROCEDURE IS PHYSICAL BATTERY DISCONNECT ONLY.
}

CON { build identity }

    SRC_REV     = 6                                         ' hand-bumped whenever this file changes
    FMT_VERSION = 1                                         ' BM- record-format version
    SF_VERSION  = 1                                         ' sign-off format (VISIT-SIGNOFF-DESIGN.md sec B.1)

CON { timing }

    CLK_FREQ = 270_000_000                                  ' the one clock line bench-run.sh patches
    _clkfreq = CLK_FREQ
    MS_PER_SEC = 1_000
    US_PER_SEC = 1_000_000
    TICKS_PER_MS = CLK_FREQ / MS_PER_SEC
    TICKS_PER_US = CLK_FREQ / US_PER_SEC

    ' p2kbSpin2Waitms: a waitms() argument must stay at or under $8000_0000 clocks. Unsigned divide,
    '  since $8000_0000 is negative as a signed long. 7_953 ms at 270 MHz, 7_158 at 300, 10_737 at 200.
    WAITMS_MAX_MS = $8000_0000 +/ (CLK_FREQ / MS_PER_SEC)

    ' every waitms() argument in this file is one of these five, each far under WAITMS_MAX_MS
    SAMPLE_MS         = 5                                   ' cog-0 poll cadence of every beat-polled loop
    OPER_POLL_MS      = 50                                  ' operator loops, under PC_KEY's ~100 ms latch
    INST_EXIT_POLL_MS = 50                                  ' the instrument's parked loop after EXIT
    WD_POLL_MS        = 250                                 ' watchdog sample cadence
    WD_IDLE_MS        = 1_000                               ' idle-forever chunk

CON { build variant -- the part, from one #ifdef chain, never a runtime test }

  ' Part built into this image (design sec 4.1):
  '  PART_NONE  - no part flag: no segment runs
  '  PART_A     - PREFLT, STOPMODE, LIVE, LADDER
  '  PART_CLOCK - PREFLT, CLOCK (built three times, at 200/270/300 MHz)
  '  PART_B     - PREFLT, FAULTB, OVERSHT
  '  PART_BRAKE - OUTSIDE (attended: one hand-brake)
  '  PART_C     - PREFLT, BASELINE, POSTFLT
  '  PART_FLOOR - FLOOR (attended: wheels down, brief observation)
  '  PART_UICHECK - UICHECK (attended: every panel control and attended screen, no motor control at all)
    #0, PART_NONE, PART_A, PART_CLOCK, PART_B, PART_BRAKE, PART_C, PART_FLOOR, PART_UICHECK
    PART_COUNT = PART_UICHECK + 1

  ' RUN_TIME_CAP_S per load (design sec 4.2 item 6)
#ifdef DUAL_PART_A
    PART_ID        = PART_A
    RUN_TIME_CAP_S = 1_500
#else
#ifdef DUAL_PART_CLOCK
    PART_ID        = PART_CLOCK
    RUN_TIME_CAP_S = 300
#else
#ifdef DUAL_PART_B
    PART_ID        = PART_B
    RUN_TIME_CAP_S = 1_200
#else
#ifdef DUAL_PART_BRAKE
    PART_ID        = PART_BRAKE
    RUN_TIME_CAP_S = 600
#else
#ifdef DUAL_PART_C
    PART_ID        = PART_C
    RUN_TIME_CAP_S = 900
#else
#ifdef DUAL_PART_FLOOR
    PART_ID        = PART_FLOOR
    RUN_TIME_CAP_S = 600
#else
#ifdef DUAL_PART_UICHECK
    PART_ID        = PART_UICHECK
    RUN_TIME_CAP_S = 1_500
#else
    PART_ID        = PART_NONE
    RUN_TIME_CAP_S = 60
#endif
#endif
#endif
#endif
#endif
#endif
#endif


CON { bench target -- the fixed dual 6.5in Rev B 18.5V rig }

' Library constants, legal under every config block (test_bench_scan.spin2's pattern), so this file
' compiles under the end-user config too. Board detection is never forced (I12).
    LEFT_TEST_BASE  = wheelL.PINS_P32_P47                   ' the LEFT board is at P32, measured 2026-09-11
    RIGHT_TEST_BASE = wheelL.PINS_P16_P31
    TEST_VOLTAGE    = wheelL.PWR_18p5V
    TEST_DET_MODE   = wheelL.BRD_AUTO_DET
    MAX_COG_ID      = 7                                     ' start() returns a cog id 0..7 on success

    ' driver state and board aliases (names, not copies, of the motor object's enums)
    DCS_UNKNOWN  = wheelL.DCS_Unknown
    DCS_STOPPED  = wheelL.DCS_STOPPED
    DCS_AT_SPEED = wheelL.DCS_AT_SPEED
    DCS_SPIN_DN  = wheelL.DCS_SPIN_DN
    DCS_FAULTED  = wheelL.DCS_FAULTED
    DCS_ESTOP    = wheelL.DCS_ESTOP
    DCS_MAX      = wheelL.DCS_ESTOP                         ' highest DCS_* value, 0..7

    ' hall inputs: plain inputs at base+5..base+7, read with pinread() (never a smart pin)
    HALL_PIN_OFFSET = 5
    HALL_PIN_SPAN   = 2                                     ' addpins operand: 3 pins
    HALL_CODE_BITS  = 3
    HALL_CODE_ILLEGAL_LO = %000
    HALL_CODE_ILLEGAL_HI = %111
    HALL_TICKS_PER_REV = 90                                 ' 6.5in motor (isp_bldc_motor hallTicInfoForMotor)

CON { drive increments and powers }

' isp_bldc_motor.spin2 confgurePowerLimits(): 147_000_000 is the 18.5V ceiling. Only the ladder's two
' probe rungs exceed it (open question Q2, ruled keep): LADDER_MAX_INCRE bounds every command.
    DRIVE_CEILING_INCRE = 147_000_000
    QTR_SPEED_INCRE     = DRIVE_CEILING_INCRE / 4           ' 36_750_000
    HALF_SPEED_INCRE    = DRIVE_CEILING_INCRE / 2           ' 73_500_000
    PREFLIGHT_INCRE     = DRIVE_CEILING_INCRE / 8           ' 18_375_000
    LIVE_TOP_INCRE      = 110_250_000                       ' LIVE's third rung, 75 %
    CLOCK_RUNG_INCRE    = 75_000_000                        ' plan T1-4 :790
    FB_INCRE            = 110_250_000                       ' FAULTB trial command, 75 %
    LADDER_MAX_INCRE    = 165_000_000                       ' the top probe rung
    LADDER_BASE_RUNGS   = 10                                ' 5 .. 147 x 10^6
    LADDER_PROBES       = 2                                 ' 155, 165 x 10^6 (Q2: kept)
    LADDER_RUNGS        = LADDER_BASE_RUNGS + LADDER_PROBES
    LADDER_FAULT_STOP   = 2                                 ' consecutive faulted rungs end a sign's ladder
    FB_TRIALS           = 5                                 ' ramp_inc 22, 100, 500, 2_000, 10_000
    STOPMODE_REPS       = 2
    STOPMODE_SPEEDS     = 2                                 ' QTR, HALF
    LIVE_RUNGS          = 3                                 ' QTR, HALF, LIVE_TOP_INCRE
    LIVE_INSTLIVE_RUNG  = 0                                 ' R14-DUAL-INSTLIVE-A is judged at the QTR rung
    CLOCK_RUNG_IDX      = 0                                 ' BM-RUNG rung of CLOCK's single rung
    OVERSHT_DISTS       = 2                                 ' 2 ft, 10 ft
    SIGN_NEG            = -1                                ' every signed loop runs NEG then POS
    SIGN_POS            = 1
    SIGN_STEP           = 2
    FAULT_PROVOKE_NEG_DEG = 3                               ' POSTFLT's fault-provoking offset_fwd
    STEER_POWER_HALF    = 50                                ' OUTSIDE driveAtPower(50, 50)
    FLOOR_POWER         = 50                                ' FLOOR driveDirection(50, +50)
    FLOOR_DIRECTION     = 50
    OVERSHT_FT_SHORT    = 2
    OVERSHT_FT_LONG     = 10
    OVERSHT_REPS        = 2
    OVERSHT_POWER       = 75                                ' setMaxSpeedForDistance(); the library default (DRIVE-OBJECTS.md:61), sec 12.8
    ' DERIVED with the steering object's own arithmetic (design sec 4.4 OVERSHT): 576 x 10^-2 mm per tick
    OVERSHT_TGT_SHORT   = 105                               ' 60_960 / 576
    OVERSHT_TGT_LONG    = 529                               ' 304_800 / 576

    ' ramp defaults (isp_bldc_motor.spin2 init()), restored and read back after every FAULTB trial (I11)
    RAMP_DEF_MIN  = 1_500
    RAMP_DEF_MAX  = 200_000
    RAMP_DEF_INC  = 22
    RAMP_DEF_DOWN = 50_000

    ' C-1 prediction pred_x10 = incre x 12_000 x 10 / 2^32, in two steps inside a long (design sec 3.2)
    PRED_INCRE_DIV = 1_000
    PRED_MUL       = 120
    PRED_DIV       = 4_295

    ' C-6 wiring-drop bound constants, printed in BM-BUILD (design sec 5.3)
    RWIRE_MOHM = 20
    PACK_MV    = 18_500

    ' frame count expected at each swept clock (isp_bldc_motor.spin2:310; study :208-212)
    CLK_SWEEP_200 = 200_000_000
    CLK_SWEEP_270 = 270_000_000
    CLK_SWEEP_300 = 300_000_000
    EXP_FRAME_200 = 4_545
    EXP_FRAME_270 = 6_136
    EXP_FRAME_300 = 6_818

CON { segment timing }

    READY_TIMEOUT_MS      = 2_000                           ' driver cog reports ready after start()
    START_SPACING_MS      = 500                             ' never two starts closer than this
    ZERO_WINDOW_MS        = 1_000                           ' floated zero-command capture per lifetime
    PREFLIGHT_MS          = 700                             ' preflight nudge
    STEADY_TIMEOUT_MS     = 4_000                           ' STOPMODE / LIVE AT_SPEED bound
    LADDER_STEADY_MS      = 6_000                           ' LADDER / OUTSIDE AT_SPEED bound
    SETTLE_MS             = 1_000
    LADDER_SETTLE_MS      = 500
    LIVE_SETTLE_MS        = 1_500                           ' the ~1 s rpm window fills
    WINDOW_MS             = 1_000
    CURRENT_POLL_MS       = 20                              ' getCurrent() during a ladder window
    REST_CONFIRM_MS       = 300                             ' pos and hwPos unchanged this long = at rest
    STOP_TIMEOUT_MS       = 3_000
    RESTART_REST_MS       = 500                             ' recovery step 3 rest
    FAULT_COOL_MS         = 5_000                           ' after any fault (scan :374)
    FAULT_TRIAL_COOL_MS   = 10_000                          ' FAULTB, open question Q3 default
    FB_TIMEOUT_MS         = 6_000
    FB_AT_SPEED_HOLD_MS   = 500
    POSTFLT_NO_FAULT_MS   = 2_000
    OVERSHT_WAIT_MS       = 12_000
    OVERSHT_HOLD_MS       = 500
    OVERSHT_MOVE_MS       = 2_000                           ' both wheels leave DCS_STOPPED after driveForDistance()
    COMMAND_SEEN_MS       = 20                              ' a new rung command reaches the mirror before AT_SPEED is read
    US_PER_MS             = 1_000
    OPER_START_TIMEOUT_MS = 120_000
    OPER_ANSWER_TIMEOUT_MS = 120_000                        ' FLOOR's which-way question
    BRAKE_WAIT_MS         = 30_000
    S5_UNTOUCHED_MS       = 5_000
    Z_STEP_MS             = 2_000
    OUT_POLL_MS           = 100
    FLOOR_RUN_MS          = 2_000                           ' brief wheels-down observation of which way the platform turns, finding AC; design sec 12.1 Q10
    UI_STEP_TIMEOUT_MS    = 30_000                          ' UICHECK: the longest wait for one control or one screen
    UI_HILITE_MS          = 500                             ' UICHECK: a received control stays highlighted this long
    UI_PREVIEWS           = 7                               ' UICHECK: attended screens shown for the operator to read
    RATE_X10_SCALE        = 10_000                          ' ticks * this / ms = ticks per second x10
    X10                   = 10

CON { instrument cog (design sec 2) }

    INST_RATE_HZ        = 500                               ' 2 ms, plan T1-1's poll period
    INST_PERIOD_TICKS   = CLK_FREQ / INST_RATE_HZ           ' 540_000 at 270 MHz
    INST_LATE_TICKS     = INST_PERIOD_TICKS / 4             ' a sample later than this is late
    INST_PERIOD_US      = US_PER_SEC / INST_RATE_HZ
    ' the smallest slack the instrument will waitct() on: below it the target could pass before
    '  waitct() runs, which would wait for the counter to wrap (~15.9 s at 270 MHz)
    INST_MIN_SLACK_US   = 200
    INST_DECIM_MAX      = 20
    FLOOR_DECIM         = 10                                ' OUTSIDE and FLOOR: 20 ms
    INST_SAMPLE_LONGS   = 9
    INST_RING_SAMPLES   = 4_096                             ' 8.19 s at 500 Hz
    INST_RING_LONGS     = INST_SAMPLE_LONGS * INST_RING_SAMPLES   ' 147_456 bytes
    INST_STACK_LONGS    = 128                               ' P2AN006 start value; scratch lives in VAR
    INST_ACK_TIMEOUT_MS = 100
    INST_STALL_MS       = 100
    INST_MOTORS         = 2

    ' one sample: +0 t, then per motor (LEFT at +1, RIGHT at +5): pos, sense, flags, hwPos
    SMP_T           = 0
    SMP_MOTOR_BASE  = 1
    SMP_MOTOR_LONGS = 4
    SMP_POS         = 0
    SMP_SENSE       = 1
    SMP_FLAGS       = 2
    SMP_HW          = 3

    ' sense long: i (i16) << 16 | phase sum (i16); flags long: duty << 16 | err << 8 | state << 5 |
    '  fault << 4 | up << 3 | integDelta
    SENSE_I_SHIFT    = 16
    SENSE_PH_MASK    = $FFFF
    SENSE_PH_SIGNBIT = 15
    FIELD_I16_MAX    = 32_767
    FIELD_DUTY_MAX   = 65_535
    FIELD_ERR_MIN    = -128
    FIELD_ERR_MAX    = 127
    FIELD_BYTE_MASK  = $FF
    FIELD_ERR_SIGNBIT = 7
    FLAG_DUTY_SHIFT  = 16
    FLAG_ERR_SHIFT   = 8
    FLAG_STATE_SHIFT = 5
    FLAG_STATE_MASK  = %111
    FLAG_FAULT_BIT   = 4
    FLAG_UP_BIT      = 3
    FLAG_IG_MASK     = %111
    INTEG_DELTA_MAX  = 7

    TRACE_PRE_SAMPLES   = 50                                ' history kept before the mark
    TRACE_MAX_SAMPLES   = 4_000                             ' 8.0 s
    TRACE_DENSE_SAMPLES = 250                               ' 0.5 s after the mark, every sample
    TRACE_DENSE_MIN     = 100                               ' sec 12.4: the dense window shrinks to this first
    TRACE_SPARSE_EVERY  = 25                                ' 50 ms
    TRACE_EMIT_MAX      = 400                               ' sec 12.4 per-trace line cap
    TRACE_STRIDE_MAX    = 8                                 ' strides 1, 2, 4, 8
    TRACE_STRIDE_GROWTH = 2
    ' post-mark capture bound: TRACE_MAX_SAMPLES less the pre-samples and the few samples a freeze may land
    '  after the wait ends, so a capture never drops samples (R14-DUAL-TRACES-*) and its mark stays in the ring
    TRACE_FREEZE_MARGIN = 25
    OVERSHT_DECIM       = 2                                 ' OVERSHT captures up to ~14.5 s: 4 ms samples fit
    ' BM-OUT buffer (design sec 4.4 OUTSIDE): one row per OUT_POLL_MS since the fault mark, across the
    '  untouched window, Z step 1, Z step 2's stop wait and Z step 2's drive, plus a margin for the
    '  command calls between the steps; a full buffer stores no further row
    OUT_POLL_SPAN_MS    = S5_UNTOUCHED_MS + Z_STEP_MS + STOP_TIMEOUT_MS + Z_STEP_MS
    OUT_POLL_MARGIN     = 10
    OUT_POLLS           = (OUT_POLL_SPAN_MS / OUT_POLL_MS) + OUT_POLL_MARGIN      ' 130
    OUT_LONGS           = 12

  ' Instrument commands (cog 0 writes):
  '  INST_CMD_NONE   - nothing commanded yet
  '  INST_CMD_ARM    - arg0 source, arg1 decimate: clear the capture, start storing
  '  INST_CMD_FREEZE - arg0 post-samples: store that many more, then stop storing
  '  INST_CMD_IDLE   - stop storing and stop reading any wheel
  '  INST_CMD_EXIT   - stop reading, park forever
    #0, INST_CMD_NONE, INST_CMD_ARM, INST_CMD_FREEZE, INST_CMD_IDLE, INST_CMD_EXIT

  ' Instrument states (the instrument writes):
  '  INST_ST_IDLE   - reads no wheel, stores nothing
  '  INST_ST_RUN    - reads the source, stores every decimated sample
  '  INST_ST_FREEZE - storing its post-samples; the FREEZE command is acked when they are done
  '  INST_ST_FROZEN - reads the source (mirror and heartbeat stay current), stores nothing
  '  INST_ST_EXITED - parked; safe to cogstop
    #0, INST_ST_IDLE, INST_ST_RUN, INST_ST_FREEZE, INST_ST_FROZEN, INST_ST_EXITED
    INST_ST_COUNT = 5

  ' Instrument source:
  '  INST_SRC_NONE   - no status block is read (hall pins only)
  '  INST_SRC_WHEELS - wheelL / wheelR
  '  INST_SRC_STEER  - the steering object's pass-throughs
    #0, INST_SRC_NONE, INST_SRC_WHEELS, INST_SRC_STEER

  ' cog-0 safety monitor result (design sec 2.8):
  '  SAFE_NONE       - nothing to act on
  '  SAFE_FAULT      - a watched motor's fault flag is set
  '  SAFE_ABS_ABORT  - ABS_ABORT_SAMPLES consecutive reads at or above ABS_ABORT_MV; the wheel was stopped
  '  SAFE_INST_STALL - the instrument heartbeat did not advance for INST_STALL_MS
    #0, SAFE_NONE, SAFE_FAULT, SAFE_ABS_ABORT, SAFE_INST_STALL

CON { safety thresholds }

    ABS_ABORT_MV      = 1_500                               ' 10 A at 150 mV/A (scan :482)
    ABS_ABORT_SAMPLES = 4
    RUN_FAULT_CAP     = 40
    LIVE_MIN_TICKS    = 49                                  ' half the MEASURED 98.2 ticks/s
    LIVE_HW_TOLERANCE = 2                                   ' |ticks - hw_ticks| allowed at INSTLIVE

CON { record widths and token lengths }

    ' clamp widths: aliases of the shared builder's own constants
    LIM_TINY  = benchLog.LIM_TINY
    LIM_SMALL = benchLog.LIM_SMALL
    LIM_MID   = benchLog.LIM_MID
    LIM_BIG   = benchLog.LIM_BIG

    TOKMAX_SEG       = 8
    TOKMAX_MOTOR     = 5
    TOKMAX_BOARD     = 7
    TOKMAX_STATE     = 10
    TOKMAX_INSTEV    = 7
    TOKMAX_INSTST    = 7
    TOKMAX_PART      = 5
    TOKMAX_CFG       = 5
    TOKMAX_FRAME     = 5
    TOKMAX_FINDS     = 24
    TOKMAX_WHY       = 18
    TOKMAX_RESULT    = 14
    TOKMAX_CAUSE     = 9
    TOKMAX_REQMODE   = 5
    TOKMAX_TEND      = 10
    TOKMAX_RST       = 9
    TOKMAX_STEP      = 8
    TOKMAX_ACTION    = 13
    TOKMAX_REASON    = 12
    TOKMAX_SCOPE     = 5
    TOKMAX_STAT      = 7
    TOKMAX_ANSWER    = 8
    TOKMAX_INPUT     = 5
    TOKMAX_SLOWER    = 5
    TOKMAX_STOPBY    = 8
    TOKMAX_PROMPT    = 10
    TOKMAX_OPEREV    = 8
    TOKMAX_SEGEV     = 5
    TOKMAX_EXIT      = 8
    TOKMAX_CP        = 10
    TOKMAX_TASK      = 5
    TOKMAX_BIN       = 6
    TOKMAX_CELL      = 20
    TOKMAX_CRIT      = 18
    TOKMAX_UNITS     = 8
    TOKMAX_SFVERDICT = 9
    TOKMAX_UIKIND    = 7
    TOKMAX_UIRES     = 7
    TOKMAX_BUTTON    = 8

CON { record enums -- each value has a token in the DAT token tables }

  ' Motor side:
  '  SIDE_NONE  - no motor (run-level records)
  '  SIDE_LEFT  - wheelL, instrument slot 0
  '  SIDE_RIGHT - wheelR, instrument slot 1
  '  SIDE_BOTH  - the steering object
    #0, SIDE_NONE, SIDE_LEFT, SIDE_RIGHT, SIDE_BOTH
    SLOT_LEFT  = 0
    SLOT_RIGHT = 1

  ' Segment (token = the name after SEG_):
    #0, SEG_NONE, SEG_PREFLT, SEG_STOPMODE, SEG_LIVE, SEG_LADDER, SEG_CLOCK, SEG_FAULTB, SEG_OVERSHT, ...
        SEG_OUTSIDE, SEG_BASELINE, SEG_POSTFLT, SEG_FLOOR, SEG_UICHECK
    SEG_COUNT = 13

  ' why (design sec 3.1); token = the name after WHY_:
    #0, WHY_NONE, WHY_NO_COG, WHY_NOT_REACHED, WHY_FAULTED, WHY_STEADY_TIMEOUT, WHY_WINDOW_TIMEOUT, ...
        WHY_STOP_TIMEOUT, WHY_NO_SAMPLES, WHY_NO_FAULT, WHY_ABORTED, WHY_INST_NOACK, WHY_INST_STALLED, ...
        WHY_INST_BUSY, WHY_RING_LOST_HEAD, WHY_MOTOR_RETIRED, WHY_OPERATOR_SKIP, WHY_OPERATOR_TIMEOUT, ...
        WHY_NO_PASSTHROUGH, WHY_UNSWEPT_CLOCK, WHY_LADDER_STOPPED, WHY_SYNC_PRECOND, WHY_NO_EXTERNAL_V, ...
        WHY_NO_EXTERNAL_I, WHY_NO_TEMP_SENSOR, WHY_PART_NOT_BUILT
    WHY_COUNT = 25

  ' BM-INST event:
    #0, INST_EV_START, INST_EV_STOP, INST_EV_NOSTART, INST_EV_NOACK
    INST_EV_COUNT = 4

  ' BM-RUNG / BM-FBTRIAL result:
    #0, RES_OK, RES_FAULT, RES_STEADY_TIMEOUT, RES_WINDOW_TIMEOUT, RES_NO_COG, RES_ABORT_I, RES_SKIPPED
    RES_COUNT = 7

  ' trace cause (what was DONE; never what the wheel did afterwards, I7):
    #0, CAUSE_STOPCMD, CAUSE_STOPCOG, CAUSE_FAULT, CAUSE_ESTOP, CAUSE_RAMP, CAUSE_DISTANCE, ...
        CAUSE_BRAKEHAND, CAUSE_FLOOR
    CAUSE_COUNT = 8

  ' requested stop mode (what was REQUESTED, I7):
    #0, MODE_FLOAT, MODE_BRAKE
    MODE_COUNT = 2

  ' BM-TRACE-END end:
    #0, TEND_REST, TEND_TIMEOUT, TEND_FAULT, TEND_ABORT, TEND_FROZEN
    TEND_COUNT = 5

  ' BM-FBTRIAL rst:
    #0, RST_NONE, RST_RESET, RST_RESTART, RST_FAILED
    RST_COUNT = 4

  ' BM-RECOVER step:
    #0, RSTEP_RESET, RSTEP_RESTART
    RSTEP_COUNT = 2

  ' BM-ABORT reason (NO_MOTION and FAULT_CAP added to the design's four, see file notes):
    #0, ABR_ABS_CURRENT, ABR_INST_STALLED, ABR_TIME_CAP, ABR_SYNC_PRECOND, ABR_NO_MOTION, ABR_FAULT_CAP
    ABR_COUNT = 6

  ' BM-ABORT scope:
    #0, SCOPE_TRIAL, SCOPE_SEG, SCOPE_RUN
    SCOPE_COUNT = 3

  ' BM-FLOOR / BM-OPER answer:
    #0, ANS_LEFT, ANS_RIGHT, ANS_STRAIGHT, ANS_NOMOVE, ANS_NONE
    ANS_COUNT = 5

  ' operator input:
    #0, INPUT_KEY, INPUT_MOUSE, INPUT_NONE
    INPUT_COUNT = 3

  ' BM-FLOOR slower wheel:
    #0, SLOWER_LEFT, SLOWER_RIGHT, SLOWER_EQUAL
    SLOWER_COUNT = 3

  ' BM-FLOOR stop_by:
    #0, STOPBY_TIMER, STOPBY_OPERATOR, STOPBY_ABORT
    STOPBY_COUNT = 3

  ' BM-OPER prompt:
    #0, PROMPT_BRAKE_L, PROMPT_FLOOR, PROMPT_UICHECK
    PROMPT_COUNT = 3

  ' BM-UISTEP kind (UICHECK):
  '  UIK_CLICK   - one live button, taken only as a mouse click
  '  UIK_KEY     - one live button, taken only as its key
  '  UIK_PREVIEW - one attended screen; START when it reads right, SKIP when it does not
    #0, UIK_CLICK, UIK_KEY, UIK_PREVIEW
    UIK_COUNT = 3

  ' BM-UISTEP result:
  '  UIR_OK      - the control arrived, or the screen read right
  '  UIR_WRONG   - the operator said the screen is wrong (SKIP)
  '  UIR_TIMEOUT - nothing usable arrived within UI_STEP_TIMEOUT_MS
    #0, UIR_OK, UIR_WRONG, UIR_TIMEOUT
    UIR_COUNT = 3

  ' BM-OPER event:
  '  OPEV_SHOWN   - a prompt the operator now sees
  '  OPEV_START   - START chosen
  '  OPEV_SKIP    - SKIP chosen
  '  OPEV_TIMEOUT - the prompt's wait ran out
  '  OPEV_ANSWER  - a FLOOR answer chosen
  '  OPEV_DONE    - the attended sequence ended; why names a short end
  '  OPEV_STOP    - STOP chosen during the FLOOR run
    #0, OPEV_SHOWN, OPEV_START, OPEV_SKIP, OPEV_TIMEOUT, OPEV_ANSWER, OPEV_DONE, OPEV_STOP
    OPEV_COUNT = 7

  ' BM-SEG event:
    #0, SEGEV_BEGIN, SEGEV_END, SEGEV_SKIP
    SEGEV_COUNT = 3

  ' BM-END exit:
    #0, EXIT_COMPLETE, EXIT_ABORTED, EXIT_WATCHDOG
    EXIT_COUNT = 3

  ' BM-OUT status (from DS_*):
    #0, STAT_MOVING, STAT_HOLDING, STAT_OFF, STAT_UNKNOWN
    STAT_COUNT = 4

  ' BM-OUT buffer, one row per poll: OUT_LONGS longs in this order
    #0, OUT_T_MS, OUT_L_STAT, OUT_R_STAT, OUT_L_ST, OUT_R_ST, OUT_L_FLT, OUT_L_SIG, OUT_R_FLT, ...
        OUT_R_SIG, OUT_TURNING, OUT_L_PWR, OUT_R_PWR

CON { cog-0 progress checkpoints -- watchdog heartbeat contract (design sec 4.3) }

' Every loop beats once per pass; every library call is bracketed by the same CP_LIB_* before and after;
' emitRecord() is bracketed by CP_EMIT.
    #0, CP_INIT, CP_INST_ACK, CP_LOOP_READY, CP_LOOP_ZERO, CP_LOOP_ATSPEED, CP_LOOP_SETTLE, ...
        CP_LOOP_WINDOW, CP_LOOP_CAPTURE, CP_LOOP_REST, CP_LOOP_STOPPED, CP_LOOP_COOL, CP_LOOP_DRAIN, ...
        CP_LOOP_OPER, CP_LOOP_POLL, CP_LIB_START, CP_LIB_STOP, CP_LIB_COMMAND, CP_LIB_QUERY, ...
        CP_LIB_OFFSETS, CP_LIB_RAMP, CP_LIB_HOLD, CP_LIB_ESTOP, CP_LIB_RESETFAULT, CP_LIB_STEER_START, ...
        CP_LIB_STEER_DRIVE, CP_LIB_STEER_STOP, CP_LIB_STEER_QUERY, CP_EMIT, CP_PANEL
    CP_COUNT = 29

CON { watchdog cog }

' WD_STALL_MS sits above every legitimate un-beaten gap (DERIVED, design sec 4.3): testResetFault() <=
' 2_030 ms; steering.driveForDistance() about 400 ms; steering.start() 100 ms.
    WD_STALL_MS       = 4_000
    WD_STACK_LONGS    = 128
    WD_STACK_SENTINEL = $5A5A_5A5A

CON { sign-off cells -- manifest row 14, task 3508 (design sec 5.2) }

    ' COUNT limits
    IDLE_UP_LO        = 0
    IDLE_UP_HI        = 0
    NOT_REVB_LO       = 0
    NOT_REVB_HI       = 0
    INTEG_SUM_LO      = 0
    INTEG_SUM_HI      = 0
    TRACE_LOST_LO     = 0
    TRACE_LOST_HI     = 0
    RESET_UNCLEAR_LO  = 0
    RESET_UNCLEAR_HI  = 0
    SIGNOFF_ONE_INSTANCE = 1

  ' Clock slot of this build (design sec 12.10). The collation lets only the latest build declaring a cell
  '  speak, so each clock build owns its cells; a CON comparison (TRUE -1, FALSE 0) selects the slot at
  '  compile time, so exactly one term below is non-zero at a swept clock and every term is zero otherwise:
  '  SF_CLOCK_UNSWEPT - CLK_FREQ is none of the three swept clocks
  '  SF_CLOCK_200     - CLK_FREQ is CLK_SWEEP_200
  '  SF_CLOCK_270     - CLK_FREQ is CLK_SWEEP_270
  '  SF_CLOCK_300     - CLK_FREQ is CLK_SWEEP_300
    #0, SF_CLOCK_UNSWEPT, SF_CLOCK_200, SF_CLOCK_270, SF_CLOCK_300
    SF_CLOCK_SLOT = 0 - (((CLK_FREQ == CLK_SWEEP_200) * SF_CLOCK_200) + ((CLK_FREQ == CLK_SWEEP_270) * SF_CLOCK_270) + ((CLK_FREQ == CLK_SWEEP_300) * SF_CLOCK_300))

    ' this build judges sign-off cells (TRUE) or none (FALSE): every part but PART_NONE, and the CLOCK part
    '  only at a swept clock. The one test every declaration and emission site uses (emitSignoffDecls(),
    '  emitSignoffs(), declareStall())
    SF_JUDGES_CELLS = (PART_ID <> PART_NONE) & ((PART_ID <> PART_CLOCK) | (SF_CLOCK_SLOT <> SF_CLOCK_UNSWEPT))

    ' R14-DUAL-DBGMASK-*: the quiet set, from the compiled user config's own channel names (sec 12.6)
    QUIET_DBG_MASK = DECOD user.DBGCH_ERROR | DECOD user.DBGCH_WARNING

